{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>advanced in days</b> — A person in the days of his youth is called \"standing in the days,\" and they are called \"his days,\" for they belong to him, as in the language of \"I will fill the number of your days\" (Exodus 23:26). But when he grows old and lives many days beyond the majority of the people of his generation, he is called \"advanced in days\" (בָּא בַּיָּמִים), because he is like one who comes to another land, journeying from city to city, from day to day." "<b>the way of women had ceased to be for Sarah</b> — This is the time of pregnancy, for after the cessation of the way [of women] due to old age she would not conceive."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:55.713797385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}